Z||000021||DecadenceR||07-12-2001||11:19 AM||||When I was coming home from Ohio once, i stopped to get gas on the PA Turnpike. It was in my 87 coupe. The lady inside the place asked me who I insured it from. She said she had bought one for ehr daughter, but had to sell it because whatever insurance company she tried going though refused to give her a policy for it, because "they're too unreliable and fire-prone".<P>My dad just learned from me the other day that yes, the Fiero's DID come in 6 cyl.... And he didn't quite believe me until I took him outside and physically showed him the 6 in my parts car.||||reg||1
Z||000022||StuGood||07-12-2001||11:52 AM||||Well, strangely enough, it's kind of nice to know I'm not the <B>only</B> one that has to deal with people who are both ignorant, <B>and</B> unaware of their ignorance.<P>You just kind of have to let the wind blow by you as they vent their ignorance, smile sympathetically, shake your head, and return to the subject at hand...  "Now, then - about those oil filters you tell me no one makes anymore...  after you look them up in the book and <B>find</B> them... I'd like to have three, please."||||reg||6
