Z||000024||Fierochic88||07-12-2001||12:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Denny:<BR><B>The local Advance people roll their eyes when I say "Pontiac Fiero."<P>American Speed Center people ignore me.<P>I get the best service from a local performance machine shop, and from Pep Boys.<P>When I need a part from the local dealers I look up the PN first, then give them that when I call or stop. Otherwise they say, "Sorry, we don't carry Fiero parts anymore."<P>I learned to deal with it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Man I love Advance.  I wouldn't shop anywhere else.  Anytime one of my Fiero friends goes in there the people who work there always say..."do you know that guy that has 10 Fieros..."  Of course they're talking about my dad.  He's become some sort of legend of craziness down there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Jennifer<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000025||b lo 0||07-12-2001||12:36 PM||||Some of my friends are like "When are you gonna sell that piece o crap?"  and I tell them "I'll sell it when you can keep up with me down Temple Johnson (REALLY twisty road here, lotsa fun)."  I haven't sold it yet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  My girlfriend likes it, and my best friend is actually jealous-and he drives a nice '85 Jeep CJ7.  He likes the sound.  I've had people say, "Oh, yeah, those things are fire traps."  I say "Those were the 4 cylinders, genius."  But the most annoying one is:<P>"Oh, you drive the <FONT COLOR="red">RUBBERMAID</FONT> car!!!"<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">      <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000026||Formula88||07-12-2001||12:56 PM||||Yeah.  I had a similar experience when I went to Pep Boys to get some gaskets for my Formula.  I tell him it's for a Fiero, and he says, "I'm sorry."  To which I replied, I bet you're sorry.  Sorry you just lost all my business because of your big mouth.  Still, my dad has that beat when he took his '61 Corvair in for an inspection....<BR>Kid gets in car....looks around.... <BR>  "Where's the ignition switch?"<BR>On the dash.  <BR>   "Oh"<BR>...looks around<BR>   "Where's the gear shift?"<BR>On the dash.<BR>   "Oh"<BR>...car lurches...kid looks around....<BR>   "Where's the parking brake?"<BR>The lever under the dash.<BR>   "Oh"<P>And when he finally gets the inspection done, he comes out and also tells me that they added a quart of antifreeze and that's an extra $5.  So, WHERE exactly did you put the antifreeze, numbnut?  Turns out they didn't add any - just trying to rip us off, which at the time was preferable to them pouring antifreeze into the engine.  <P>Never underestimate the stupidity of the average American.||||reg||1
Z||000027||Leadfoot||07-12-2001||02:58 PM||||Well I called a local Goodyear alignment shop and asked them if they can align my fiero.  The guy said sure...no problem just bring it on over.  So I brought it in 1st thing in the morning.  As I entered the guy behind the desk (who not only was the person I spoke to the day before, but is also the owner of the shop) said "you really want to ruin my day don't you.  Those cars are the biggest P.O.S. Pontiac ever made.  I don't know why you even drive it....I hate those dam cars."  I said "geez you were so polite on the phone when I called earlier...what happened?" I tried to crack a joke and said "well at least I didn't lower the car."  He just replied "if it was I wouldn't even touch it."  WTF if he had a problem with fieros why did he agree to work on it.  Nice way to attract costumers jerky!||||reg||1
