Z||000033||FieroKyle||07-12-2001||08:00 PM||||Anyone who does bad mouth my car, I automatically ask to race them with the stock 2.8, they either chicken out or see tail lights! hahaha lol. I have a date with a probe later this week for a race. =)Most people tell me how great my car is, and the few people who have drove it always ask me again to drive it. Even mt friend who has a 5.0 Stang'. he let me drive his he drove mine, I was impressed with the 5.0 even though I hate ford. Now I have a quest to put a 350 sbc in my fiero, I hope ot works out for me when I do it. lol =)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign_1.jpg"> <BR>My Fast 'n Black Car<P>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000034||jake1852||07-12-2001||08:41 PM||||heres a good one that happened to me yesterday-<P>im parked in front of napa, and this guy comes up to me and says, "why the hell would you put fiero rims on that car?!?!" and im driving a freakin' 87gt!||||reg||1
Z||000035||8Ball||07-12-2001||09:36 PM||||Back when I had my Fiero, I had a friend who drove a 94 vette. He was constantly ragging on my little beast. Little did he know I had a 350 in the back  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Finally, one day after listening to him b*tch and moan about Fiero'<BR>s while I was working on the interior of mine, I lokked and him and grinned. "If Fiero's are so crappy, I suppose you wouldn't be afraid to race for 100 bucks would ya?" He eagerly accepted the bet and laffed. He kept on laffing up to the point where I dusted him from the light, and then at the end of our 3 block race I was sitting sideways with the door open smokeing a cig waiting on him to finish  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>8Ball||||reg||1
Z||000036||Adrift||07-12-2001||10:02 PM||||I'm going to play devils advocate for a moment - Why is it that everyone thinks the Fiero is a piece of sh*t? The simple answer to this is, "well its american and its old, so its most likely a piece of **** ." But it seems as though people in general seem to dislike the Fiero more then other POS old American cars... Most of you mentioing they have never been in one, I find it very unlikely that it is a thing of jealousy. Its more likely that the only exposure they have had to the fiero is the through the general media, which has officialy titled the Fiero as a piece of sh*t due to the engine fires, which is understandable (Having fibreglass-like plastic panels which release toxic fumes when burned(melted) didn't make it any better...). <P>But then again most of the people in this forum aren't really even driving a "Fiero", considering the after-market modifications they make to the breaks, engine, etc. There were a lot of problems with the fiero, most of which have been fixed by the talented group of people present in this forum. It wasn't Pontiac that fixed these problems (Well in 88 they did but by then it was too late...), it was do-it-yourself home type people which have customized the Fiero into the fun, safe, perfectly drivable car which most of the people on this forum have learned to love.<P>(excuse broken english, I'm very tired at the moment)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000037||ferrari_momo||07-12-2001||10:10 PM||||fierochick88,<BR> hey i never got the MO from u yet.<BR>fiero_24, <BR> u got a euro tail light kit?  hmm, what lens did u use?  <BR>pat K<BR>ferrari_momo@yahoo.com<P>hahaha... the same thing happened to me at autozone.  i told the guy to take a look at my car.  showed the body work and the TA 3.4 motor in it.  he changed his mind about fiero and wanted one afterwards  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000038||FieroJoe||07-12-2001||10:22 PM||||Very very true Adrift!  Any car that is well maintained will last for a long time.<P>Very true about customization too.  Except for some here who have low mileage cars that should remain bone stock, I think that every Fiero owned my someone on this Forum has had quite a few mods done to make it either run better, look nicer, or just plain be cooler.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I have not done buisness with autozone since the dumba$$ that works there always has to make stupid comments.  And thier prices arent always the best either.  I usually go to carquest, where people actually know about cars and help out.||||reg||1
