Z||000044||qwikgta||07-13-2001||10:53 PM||||A few months after I picked up my 88 coupe I went into Jiffy Lube for a quick oil change, I didnt have the ability to take off the oilfilter, and they told me that they could not change the oil.  I asked why and they said that "they don't work on Fieros".  I have also had probs getting parts that I know are just general 2.5 engine parts that came on all GM cars. <P>Rob <P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000045||Frank Sombers||07-14-2001||12:40 AM||||bHooper:<BR>I have an '88 cpe, and my wife has an '94 Intrepid (she doesn't work at Auto Zone). Believe me, parked side by side in the garage the Intrepid is a hell of a lot bigger than the Fiero. <BR>BUT with two people in the car the interior space of the Intrepid isn't all that much greater.<BR>Frank<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000046||Conrad Sanville||07-14-2001||08:49 AM||||The jerk behind the counter was (is) an unprofessional idiot.  Cars that need parts keep these people in business.<P>Fieros always were controversial.  Any poorly maintained car from two decades ago can become POS.  Even a POS Fiero with its unusual stance stands out.<P>I've driven my '84 Fiero for going on 18 years, with almost 350K and since I am from a small town people that know me and the car and would be hard pressed to call the car a POS.<P>Folks that drive by my place in the summer do rubberneck when they see 3 shiny white Fieros in the driveway. Some have even stopped to take pictures.   <P>Anyone who has ridden in my GT are quite amazed at the car's handling and ride, especially around entrance ramps!<P>Would love to see the day when a good size Fiero club parades its cars through our town!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000047||lowCG||07-14-2001||04:17 PM||||The uninformed are always a source of amusement,like the guy in the new 540i who couldn't quite keep up,or just the people who wonder why they quit making the car after seeing the TDC motor in there and thinking that it actually came that way!<BR>I couldn't find anyone reputable to fix(blackhawk)a slightly tweaked rear frame extension recently;people really do in fact think that these cars are SO different or something,the narrow mindedness really can be pretty amazing/annoying sometimes.||||reg||1
Z||000048||grinthock||07-14-2001||04:23 PM||||Lets start the exuse list WHY people say they suck<P><BR>1)  They stopped making them because of all the problems<P>2)  They all catch on fire<P>3)  The suspension is from a chevette<P>4)  That's just a pissy old 2.8<P>5)  The only one that was ever worth looking at is the one with lotus steering but even then I wouldn't pay more than $1500||||reg||1
Z||000049||Fierowrecker||07-14-2001||08:17 PM||||Reminds me of a visit to the local MacDonalds...<BR>I had just picked up my wife's Fiero from the paint shop, so the body looked new...<BR>As I was eating my sandwich, some grunt walks up and starts to rag on me for not buying an American car...<BR>I got out and walked him to the front of the car and pointed to the imprinted headlamp cover and acted like I was reading to a moron, POOONTEEEEAAAAAC.......<BR>Musta been a new labor union inductee...<BR>Hope he could read...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
