Z||000052||The Fieromaster||07-15-2001||12:02 AM||||I have a hell of an inspection story... I was at the local emissions place and the kid drives my car on the rollers then looks under the car a little bit... He then parks the FRONT WHEELS on the rollers hits and begins his test (as i beat on the spectator window yelling "rear wheels a$$-hole")... He didnt hear.. poped the clutch and almost slammed the test places fan that blows air on the radiator!  I run outside and after a yelling fit he says...<BR>"But i didnt see a drive shaft, no drive shaft means a front wheel drive car"<BR>-the engine is in the rear so you wouldnt see a drive shaft<P>Some people make me sick, sicketty, sick, sick!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That, Wrecked Better"<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">      <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||11
Z||000053||Doni Hagan||07-15-2001||10:55 AM||||Fiero's are POS?<P>Let's see.....So far, I've owned 2 pre-Ford Jaguars, 1 mid-70's Rolls, 1 Vanden Plas Princess 4 ltr R, 1 Ferrari 306 GTS and an 85 Cadillac Seville with the 4100 engine. <P>Other than a bad brake light switch that ran my battery down, my 87 GT starts every day and has yet to have me sitting on the side of the road waiting for AAA. It's a pain in the a$$$ to work with at times, but so am I and no one's talking about junkin' me yet!<P> <P>||||reg||6
Z||000054||BV MotorSports||07-16-2001||11:10 PM||||When I got my 87GT back from the guy I sold it too a yr ago the clutch pedal was stuck on the floor.<BR>Checked it all out and ended up dropping the cradle. Pulled the trans and saw that the clutch fork was broken. Called the dealer and ordered a new one for $79 bucks. Picked up the phone book and started calling trans shops. Lady picks up the phone at the 1st one I called and I said "Hi, I have an 87 Fiero GT"....(cuts me off) "We dont work on them", and hangs up on me. Now since I had just dropped my cradle in the drive way in 98 deg weather and since I tend to get offened pretty easy at times, I called that "lady" (to be nice) back and told the lady that I already have the trans out and just need to get the clutch fork replaced. She says "oh, well we still dont work on fieros"! and hangs up on me again!   ^&((%&$^%%$#%$#$ Boy was I mad. <BR>Then on my way to the only shop I found (denbigh transmissions) that will work on fieros, I stop at the parts store. Now remember I am having a pretty bad day....<BR>Go into the P-Boys and ask for a clutch slave cyl. Guy looks up and says " oh, a Ferrario, those where pieces of ****  when they built them"! Thats it! I couldnt take no more. I reach up and grab the front of the guys shirt and say "WTF did you just say about my car"? He backs off and says he was just joking and to chill out. I then ask if he has ever owned one, driven one, or even had any experience with one. Awnser.....NOPE. Never!<P>Boy what a bad day that was.<P>Steven<P>*warning* if you are a parts counter jockey and I come in covered in sweat and grease on a hot and humid day and you ,setting in the A/C, make a smart a$$ comment about one of my cars....you may get that part I wanted shoved up your A$$! God help you if I look at your hands and they are smooth w/o a trace of grease under the finger nails!!!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 89mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>87 Conquest TSi 406 SBC V8!<BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||11
Z||000055||The Fieromaster||07-16-2001||11:48 PM||||GET EM STEVE!  Thats how i feel today.. My goddamn GT wil not flucking run... im gonna freak out!! AAAAHHHHH!!!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That, Wrecked Better"<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">      <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000056||AusFiero||07-17-2001||11:14 AM||||We don't have that POS stigma in Australia because Fieros are virtually unknown. All I usually cop is hot car man, cool, wish I had a car like that.<P>Now on the downside I am in the Pontiac Car Club of Australia. At the nats I am the blacksheep of the family and put up with snide remarks. Showed them but on the sprint racing. A 2.8 ltr stock Fiero can make many a 400 CI Trans Am look like a POS when ya beat em on the drag strip. Ok not all but of 55 70's TAs I got better times than 30 of them. These people have a peice POS unmaintained Trans Am and think because it is a V8 it can beat anything.<P>I also then remind the snide remark ones that hey, lets go find a windy mountain road and I will show you whos driving the POS.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
